Apologies for posting this to the osf group, but I know there are people who
read it that do threads.

I'm trying to combine DECthreads and RPC (NCS) in an application to do
distributed computing on a bunch of uni-processors (DEC 5000s w/Ultrix &
(soon) alphas w/OSF/1).  When the rpc call is made the current thread seems
to wait for it.  It doesn't yield, so I wind up with sequential distributed
computing, rather than parallel.

I've tried FIFO, RR & OTHER scheduling; controller at a higher priority
than the worker threads and vice versa for all three.  Nothing seems make
the rpc thread yield to the controller thread.  It seems rpc$sar() (in
proj_cstub.c) blocks until it gets the results back from the remote
host, and the thread isn't detecting this as a block.  I can't see
a way to insert a pthread_yield(), since I don't have (and don't really
want) access to rpc$sar().

I'm probably going to try switching my threading algorithm around.  I hope
to soon have DCE and start using it.  Maybe that'll give me more control?

Thanks for any ideas,

John
